  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kiribati-Australia Education Program in Tungaru (EduKAiT)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kiribati-Australia Education Program in Tungaru (EduKAiT) seeks to strengthen the Government of Kiribati&apos;s capacity to deliver education services and improve gender equality, disability inclusion and climate change with key objective to improve teaching and learning across Years 1-13 across Kiribati in close collaboration with Kiribati Ministry of Education. The EduKAiT program logic articulates three end of program outcomes:
EOPO1: Improved learning outcomes for boys and girls, including those with disabilities, at targeted year levels
EOPO2: Improved access, transition and completion rates for boys and girls, including those with disabilities, in a safe school environment
EOPO3: MoE delivers more efficient resource allocation through increased public financial management reform and use of data inform decision making</narrative>
  </description>
